name: Link Analysis card fraud showcase
tagline: "A seeded card and e-commerce fraud Link Analysis demo - card testing, an account-takeover ring, a colluding merchant and a compromised fuel station, planted among 6 500 cards with benign look-alikes"
description: "The card and e-commerce fraud Link Analysis demo as a Space Template, Basic tier. Six synthetic feeds (cardholder, card, merchant, card_auth, chargeback, online_account; 12 months from 2025-10-01 in data/inbox, the next month in data/staged; 5 030 cardholders, 6 500 cards, 900 merchants, 4 000 online accounts, about 77 000 authorisations) are landed by six Collectors and Pipelines. The card_links Job folds them into ONE link Dataset (src, dst, kind, ts, amount, event_date, via) of eight link kinds. Planted stories (ground truth: tools/gen-la-card-data.ground-truth.json; pinned by CardLinksJobGoldenTest and tools/gen-la-card-data.test.mjs): one device and one /24 network try 300 cards with 1.00 authorisations at three small online shops in one night, 85 % declined; 8 devices move 140 online accounts onto 5 drop addresses in seven weeks and buy on their cards; merchant M-221 refunds 12 cards it never sold to and its chargebacks run about 9x its category; 60 cards are defrauded 1-6 weeks after paying at fuel station M-317 in one 3-week window. Benign look-alikes that must not join a story: a corporate proxy network used by about 200 genuine cards, a family tablet shared by four accounts at one address, travel merchant M-140 with a chargeback spike in one strike month, and the busy supermarket M-052 whose customers are never defrauded. Four saved views. Runs on every edition, Basic included: no sign-in personas, Alert Rules or Investigations. Card ids are invented, never card numbers. Synthetic data only."
minEdition: basic
icon: heroicons_outline:credit-card
contents[5]: "6 Collectors + Pipelines + Datasets (12 months landed, 1 month staged)", "card_links Job + Dataset (8 link kinds, via)", "4 saved views (card testing, takeover ring, merchant disputes, common point of purchase)", "4 planted stories with benign look-alikes", "Ground truth and golden tests in the repository"
